; ROTATE FORTY BY FOUR  UPWARD  entered at the first byte of a forty byte
; run with four free cells immediately ABOVE it; every byte moves up four
; places and the last four wrap round to the bottom; the pointer comes back
; where it started;
;
; IT IS block/rotate40down4 RUN THE OTHER WAY  and it exists as its own file
; because an include takes no parameters and CONVENTIONS forbids control
; logic on the templating side; aes/decrypt128 writes its ten schedule temps
; with the downward turn and reads them back with this one  because the
; inverse cipher consumes them in the opposite order from the one that made
; them;
; every byte moves up four places  the highest four into the scratch above
